{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfQeGKZejZmKAfx2ebqmd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RnzctWW8bPTSGX3wjdiXiY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nattavo: build #217, drive as a pass (reconciler R2)\n\nattavo drive N becomes one short pass: it fast-forwards its working\ncopy to origin's branch (never while a worker holds it), reads the\nitem's report, and acts at most once -- recovers a dead or hung\ninvocation, or starts the next stage -- before returning within\nseconds.\n\nStarting a stage is the lease: the pass writes the invocation marker\nand pushes it as a plain fast-forward with no merge and no retry\n(push_lease); a lost race or an outright refusal both undo the local\nmarker commit and the pass starts nothing. On a pushed marker the pass\nspawns `attavo worker N <build|verify> NN` in its own session, stdout\nand stderr redirected to <git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.worker.log; the\nworker outlives the pass, runs the stage in-process, and touches\n<git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.heartbeat every ATTAVO_HEARTBEAT_S seconds\nwhile it runs. The report and the pass read alive from the heartbeat\nfirst, falling back to the invocation's pid only when there is no\nheartbeat file; the stall bound decides hung, never died, so a dead\ninvocation is recovered even with no [drive].stall_after_s declared.\n\nA review takes the forge checks the pass already read on the\npre-marker head (ATTAVO_FORGE_CHECKS); attavo verify reads that file\ninstead of polling when it is set. --again starts the next attempt of\na stopped stage; --all runs one pass in every ../attavo-worktree-N\nbeside the checkout; --until-ready repeats the pass in one process\nuntil the level is the operator's or done, a check concludes red, or\nthe checks have not concluded within ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S.\n--recover is gone and exits 2 saying so.\n\nRetires the stage run and the forge poll inside the old synchronous\n`attavo drive`, `--recover` as an operator's act, the refusal to\nrecover without a stall bound, verify's own poll when a pass has read\nthe checks, and the synchronous drive calls this repository's own\ntests made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":332635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":228},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041a92ee-b14a-4832-b613-6f5a12b6a373","uuid":"73747b2b-96e1-429e-8fb2-379c93f43c53","timestamp":"2026-09-25T18:37:52.570Z","request_id":"req_011CfQeGK6rfJVvJNAMqE6Gu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RnzctWW8bPTSGX3wjdiXiY":{"command":"cd /Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-217 && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nattavo: build #217, drive as a pass (reconciler R2)\n\nattavo drive N becomes one short pass: it fast-forwards its working\ncopy to origin's branch (never while a worker holds it), reads the\nitem's report, and acts at most once -- recovers a dead or hung\ninvocation, or starts the next stage -- before returning within\nseconds.\n\nStarting a stage is the lease: the pass writes the invocation marker\nand pushes it as a plain fast-forward with no merge and no retry\n(push_lease); a lost race or an outright refusal both undo the local\nmarker commit and the pass starts nothing. On a pushed marker the pass\nspawns `attavo worker N <build|verify> NN` in its own session, stdout\nand stderr redirected to <git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.worker.log; the\nworker outlives the pass, runs the stage in-process, and touches\n<git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.heartbeat every ATTAVO_HEARTBEAT_S seconds\nwhile it runs. The report and the pass read alive from the heartbeat\nfirst, falling back to the invocation's pid only when there is no\nheartbeat file; the stall bound decides hung, never died, so a dead\ninvocation is recovered even with no [drive].stall_after_s declared.\n\nA review takes the forge checks the pass already read on the\npre-marker head (ATTAVO_FORGE_CHECKS); attavo verify reads that file\ninstead of polling when it is set. --again starts the next attempt of\na stopped stage; --all runs one pass in every ../attavo-worktree-N\nbeside the checkout; --until-ready repeats the pass in one process\nuntil the level is the operator's or done, a check concludes red, or\nthe checks have not concluded within ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S.\n--recover is gone and exits 2 saying so.\n\nRetires the stage run and the forge poll inside the old synchronous\n`attavo drive`, `--recover` as an operator's act, the refusal to\nrecover without a stall bound, verify's own poll when a pass has read\nthe checks, and the synchronous drive calls this repository's own\ntests made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RnzctWW8bPTSGX3wjdiXiY":{"cwd":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-217"}}}
